WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.579
Caching model responses.

2
00:00:01.859 --> 00:00:14.061
Caching here means record and replay: you store each model response keyed by everything that determined it, and later runs with an identical request read the stored response instead of calling the model.

3
00:00:14.341 --> 00:00:22.021
It is different from provider prompt caching (Studio 1), which makes repeated prompt prefixes cheaper but still runs the model.

4
00:00:22.301 --> 00:00:24.584
Record and replay gives you three things.

5
00:00:24.864 --> 00:00:28.299
Speed and cost, since unchanged cases don’t pay twice.

6
00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:35.811
Determinism, since a replayed suite gives the same result every time, so any change in score was caused by your code.

7
00:00:36.091 --> 00:00:43.984
And a fixed corpus for developing graders: you can rewrite a judge prompt or a parser and rescore last night’s outputs for free.

8
00:00:44.264 --> 00:00:45.757
The hard part is the key.

9
00:00:46.037 --> 00:00:50.304
It must change whenever the output could legitimately change, and only then.

10
00:00:50.584 --> 00:01:05.667
Include the pinned model id, the full rendered system prompt and messages, every request setting that affects output (effort, max_tokens, tools and tool choice, output format), and the trial number when you sample a question several times.

11
00:01:05.947 --> 00:01:08.336
Exclude timestamps and request ids.

12
00:01:08.616 --> 00:01:13.117
Serialize with sorted keys, or two equal requests will hash differently.

13
00:01:13.397 --> 00:01:23.104
Inspect’s documented cache key covers the same ground: model name and base URL, message history, epoch, generation config, and active tools.

14
00:01:23.384 --> 00:01:34.904
Its responses expire after one week by default, and its docs recommend explicitly versioned model names so a new deployment under an alias doesn’t silently reuse old responses.

15
00:01:35.184 --> 00:01:41.200
Promptfoo caches by default too (on disk, 14 days by default), with --no-cache to bypass it.

16
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.995
Know what a cache can’t see.

17
00:01:43.275 --> 00:01:51.360
If the provider changes the model behind an alias, or a dated model behaves differently over time, a replayed suite stays green.

18
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.880
That’s why the nightly tier runs uncached.

19
00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:57.829
A sound rule: replays answer “did my code change the result?

20
00:01:58.109 --> 00:02:00.776
”, and live runs answer “did the system change?

21
00:02:01.056 --> 00:02:01.354
”.
